{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power","id":1396094,"title":"Shaping Rituals and You: A Guide To Power","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-12T18:45:28-07:00","id":1396094,"title":"Shaping Rituals and You: A Guide To Power","content":"There wasn't a good guide to shaping rituals, so I made one. It includes the Core Book, What Fire Has Wrought, and Fangs At The Gate. They are broken down by Initiation and listed with catchy names in the order they are displayed. I didn't cover any of the merits involved, just the Shaping Rituals themselves.<br /> <br /> CAVEAT: There is an assumption with this rating system: the ability to quickly cast your first in-combat Sorcery is much more important than your ability to get off your second or third spell in the scene. This is based on my personal play experience, as well as a deep dive into threads about people's experience with sorcery- namely that many Sorcerers just cast their one big spell with their Shaping Ritual and then proceed to fight with charms. This will skew toward rituals that offer a one-time power boost rather than those that offer you a slow and steady trickle of power. As always, Your Mileage May Vary.<br /> <br /> The Shaping Rituals will follow this format:<br /> <b>Name of Initiation</b><br /> <u>Name of Ritual</u>: Basic Description of Ritual<br /> Motes: How many motes you get, how you get them, and how long they last.<br /> Control: is there a bonus for control spells<br /> Opinion: a general feeling of perceived use or inherent problems.<br /> Verdict: is it worth taking.<br /> <br /> Author's Note: The &quot;value&quot; of Intimacies and Stunts comes up quite a lot. I will post those here for your ease of reference.<br /> Intimacies: 2/3/4 minor/major/defining<br /> Stunts: 1/2/3<br /> I will not be evaluating Sorcerous Merits in this post.<br /> CORE<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Bargain With Mara</b>: you boinked a sex demon. Good for you.<br /> <u>Unrequited love</u>: if you have someone with a tie of Love towards you, that you do not return, you can pull sorcerous motes from their affection. You monster.<br /> Motes: 4 for a defining, less for weaker ones.<br /> Restriction: once per person per day. No more than 10 motes per scene.<br /> Control Bonus: pull from more than one person at a time.<br /> Opinion: very weak. You need multiple unrequited loves around you to use this, and honestly it means you either worked this out with a player or you have multiple sex-flunkies around and no one wants to play with that guy. Mechanically its a poor effect, you get 4 motes from someone who is defined by their love for you, once a day.<br /> Verdict: Pass.<br /> <br /> <u>Sex Vampire</u>: You have to sex someone and then eat their soul, literally killing them. How the hell did this pass editing?<br /> Motes: Spend a bound soul for (Ess+WP) sm. You can keep (Ess+Occult) souls bound at one time.<br /> Control: Spend a soul in place of paying a willpower to cast a spell.<br /> Opinion: what the fuck is wrong with you.<br /> Mechanical Opinion: 6 to 15 motes per scene is pretty powerful, you can keep 4-10 of these on hand, and depending on your pick up game it should be easy to replenish these.<br /> Verdict: Literally no one wants to play with this at the table. I would hard ban this option and re-evaluate my relationship to anyone who wanted to take it. Mechanically it depends on how often you can bang.<br /> <br /> <u>Cast In Shadow</u>: Night Caste can Cast Too. You get free motes for being in the shadows.<br /> Motes: 3 for starting a scene in shadow. +1 ever Shape Sorcery for staying in the shadow AND the target is unaware of you. A night with no moon counts as shadow.<br /> Control: None<br /> Opinion: Designed for assassins. 3Sm to start, and the +1 is conditional. If the target is unaware of you, it probably doesn't matter how quick you can cast this.<br /> Verdict: Pass.<br /> <br /> <b>Pact With an Ifrit Lord</b>: Pyromancy with extra steps.<br /> <br /> <u>Fueled by Fire</u>: Pull sm from a fire source. Might extinguish that source.<br /> Motes: (Essence) from fire in Medium range. Torches: one time use. Bonfires: 2. Burning house: infinite. Works on Fire elementals too, if you beat their resolve.<br /> Control: Doesn't diminish the fire.<br /> Opinion: Very thematic, mechanically weak. Terrestrial Circle Sorceries cost 15sm so this is next to useless. It's weird that the size of the fire doesn't give you more motes.<br /> Verdict: This is cool fodder for stunts and memorable moments. Mechanically, however, it's quite weak.<br /> <br /> <u>Burnt Offerings</u>: throw treasure into a fire to please Flame Daddy. Relies on 3 non-sorcery stats.<br /> Motes: hope you like math. (Cha+Perf) against Diff(5-Resources burnt). Gain (Ess+Bonus Successes)<br /> Control: zilch.<br /> Opinion: this requires Charisma, Performance, Resources, and Downtime. And you lose the Resources. However, this begins the trend that Excellency-able, Storable Shaping Rituals are OP.<br /> Verdict: its only worth it if you already have a character who fits the stats and wants to splice sorcery. Otherwise, pass.<br /> <br /> <u>Burning Passion</u>: torture a metaphor to get sorcerous motes.<br /> Motes: if you would get a point of Willpower from upholding an \u201cpassionate emotion or fervent belief\u201d intimacy, turn that into 5 sm instead (lasts until sunrise). Also you can downgrade an intimacy to get points, once per day.<br /> Control: nope<br /> Opinion: it rewards a certain type of character who always goes out of their way to uphold their intimacies, like a shonen hero. But also it lets you downgrade intimacies for temporary power, so its basically like being a drug addict. I guess you could do something with that contradiction there. This requires a lot of spotlight and rp'ing a hothead character. The motes are temporary so you got to be always working this, and I could see how that requires a lot of ST-Player work and also other players to be onboard with you being a firebrand.<br /> Verdict: Its a lot of work for 5sm per scene. Pass.<br /> <br /> <b>Scarred By Nightmares</b>: Lovecraft Lite<br /> <br /> <u>Last Night I Dreamt I Went to Manderley Again</u><br /> <br /> I mean, uh,<br /> <br /> <u>Dark Dreams</u>: When you sleep, have an uneasy time of it and a dark vision.<br /> Motes: give up the willpower you get from sleeping, and roll (Wits+Occult) to get sm. Once per <b>story</b>, stunt out how you saw this in your dream and get (Ess x [Stunt+1]), yay math. Lasts until you sleep again.<br /> Control: if you spend ALL of these motes on your control spell, they count for 2x.<br /> Opinion: This certainly seems OP AF, except that you only carry the SM until you sleep again, which means you need to forgo the willpower from sleeping every night to make sure you have them. And you need WP to do sorcery so...<br /> Verdict: This ritual is is probably the best balanced one in the whole book, because its easy to carry a massive load of sm around but you also wont get back WP which is a super important resource. Powerful but not OP, thematic as hell.<br /> <br /> <u>Deranged</u>: Its not a phase, mom! This is who I am!<br /> Motes: verrrry conditional: stunt your derangement/taboo to get the Stunt rating as sm. Get 2 more if its a control spell. Lasts until sleep. Get 10 sm the first time you stunt your shaping roll with the flaw in a way that gives you Solar xp for upholding a flaw, they last until the end of the story. After that, each time you do the flaw thing gain (Ess) sm.<br /> Control: 2 more sm for the control spell<br /> Opinion: this has a lot of bookkeeping to it. Mostly though, its Stunt Rating (so 1, 2, or 3) per cast with the one time bonus of 10 motes.<br /> Verdict: if you want to play a tortured lovecraftian pc, it can be very thematic. Mechanically its too much work for too little bonus.<br /> <br /> <u>Eating Mental Anguish</u>: consume emotions for power.<br /> Motes: whenever someone else gains or loses an intimacy, you get motes for it. 2/3/4 for Minor/Major/Defining. If anyone gains Limit, you get their (Limit Rank). If someone else is in Limit Break, you can get 10sm. Lasts for the story.<br /> Control: none<br /> Opinion: Requires your party/NPCs to be gaining and losing Intimacies at a good rate, so how useful it is depends on your group. Personally this hasn't happened much at my table, but the motes last for a story, so... hard to say.<br /> Verdict: this depends entirely on your table.<br /> <br /> <b>Soul Perfecting Elixir</b>: will absolutely tell you they are Vegan.<br /> <br /> <u>Protein Shake</u>: Get mana from alchemical Bro Science<br /> Motes: Drinking a potion lets you roll for (Stam+Occult) motes. that's probably 5 without excellencies, 10 with excellencies. <br /> Control: you can make a potion that doesn't go bad ever, but only for the control spell.<br /> Opinion: <b>FIXED</b>. I had originally misread this one. It's fine, Difficulty 2 for a regular potion or Difficulty 4 to get a weeks worth, pretty easy. <br /> Verdict: Good. Difficulty 4 is an easy Craft roll and you'll almost certainly have this on hand all week, and it lasts for multiple sorceries. <br /> <br /> <u>Power of Prudes</u>: Never have fun, get SM<br /> Motes: (Stamina) motes every night of sleeping, until the next sleep. You also get 1 more mote per point of Deprivation, but deprivation is just a -3 after \u201c(Stamina) days without food, and final hours (of life) without water\u201d, which seems like it would harm your internal alchemy but what do I know. Once per story, (Ess+Stam) sm, for the whole story.<br /> Control: none<br /> Opinion: How the hell does Deprivation even work here, the -3 comes out of your Shape Sorcery roll (and EVERY OTHER ROLL TOO). Otherwise its just a flat 5 motes per day with an RP restriction of being a crossfitter.<br /> Verdict: Lame. The 5sm (for max Stam) bonus is weak and the Story Length bonus is one time use. You can also loose these if you don't live like an ascetic (which you are begging your ST to challenge). Hard Pass.<br /> <br /> <b>Talisman of 10k Eyes</b>: We saw Doctor Strange too.<br /> <br /> <u>I See You (Bojack)</u>: get sm for noticing stuff. No really.<br /> Motes: 1 for every 2 success on a JB roll, lasts for the scene. Add Occult if there are other Sorcerers or Demons.<br /> Control: None<br /> Opinion: Oh hey, free motes for what you are already doing.<br /> Verdict: Very Strong. This is basically the \u201cfree sm\u201d ritual. Ripe for MinMax abuse. If you are a combat character just dabbling in sorcery, take this one.<br /> <br /> <u>Arcane Focus (wait wrong game)</u>: get sm for using your shaping ritual.<br /> Motes: Stunt Rating +2, once a scene<br /> Control: more than once a scene.<br /> Opinion: for an RP ritual, this is bland. It's most generic white bread ritual in the game- use your ritual to get a bonus for using your ritual.<br /> Verdict: Bad. Its gonna get you between 3 and 5 sm, which sucks, but you have a magic doodad so you might as well use it.<br /> Special: This is one of the rare Shaping Rituals that let you steadily gain power, since you can use it over and over again on your control spell... but that's not really as strong as you were hoping for in the heat of battle.<br /> <br /> <u>Investment of Power</u>: Motes in, Motes out.<br /> Motes: <b>commit</b> up to 10 motes of essence, and then get (Ess+2) sm's per turn back out.<br /> Control: trade essence motes for sm's at 1:2 instead of 1:1<br /> Opinion: the committed motes are a harsh cost, because you never have enough motes in my experience. But trading them 1:2 is pretty good. However, you only get 3~7 per turn, so...<br /> Verdict: I'd probably pass this one. If you don't use a lot of motes for your build, though, it can be really good.<br /> <br /> <b>Miscellaneous</b>: these were too good to throw away but have no theme.<br /> <br /> <u>Basic Heptagram</u>: Look it up in a book.<br /> Motes: (Int + Lore), and maybe one or two more if you have a librarian on hand. For the Story.<br /> Control: No<br /> Opinion: are you really going to go to the library between every spell casting? No, no you aren't is the DB initiation before WFHW came out.<br /> Verdict: NPC only, this sucks.<br /> <br /> <u>Storm Born</u>: Powered by Thor.<br /> Motes: 2/turn in the storm, or (Essence) one time if only a little windy. 5Sm per point of damage taken by stormy environmental effects.<br /> Control: No<br /> Opinion: Yeah I saw Stormcaller in AotC too.<br /> Verdict: Situational at best. Pass unless you are the one making storms.<br /> <br /> <u>Geomancy</u>: Except its actually \u201cOwning a Manse\u201d<br /> Motes: (Ess+WP) motes, but take 1 Agg damage. Last for 2 weeks. +1 each turn if you are in the manse.<br /> Control: Seeing a theme here? No.<br /> Opinion: The Damage heals in a single day if you aren't otherwise wounded, but this is a flat 6-10 sm so neither the benefit or cost are worth much.<br /> Verdict: Its fine, I guess? It's definitely half baked.<br /> <br /> <u>Just Performance</u>: what if we took all the creativity out of using music to inspire people?<br /> Motes: (Performance) for a scene, after using Performance to influence people... in a way that matches the spell. Not a (Cha+Perf) roll, a flat bonus, and only if the spell somehow themes into your song?<br /> Control: Really? Of course not.<br /> Opinion: Did we just need to pad the word count? Unless you have a song for inspiring pyromania (Brilliant Raptor) or a song about flechetting the enemy (DoOB), what's the actual point of this? You have to move people by Performance in the scene, and find a way to match it to the spell. Its gonna lead to tortured, twisted equivocation at best.<br /> Verdict: This is just bad.<br /> Special: I know you don't need to sing. Bite me.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u>What Fire Has Wrought</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Heptagram</b>: Exalted Hogwarts AU.<br /> <br /> <u>Book Learnin'</u>: I already did this one. Told you it was weak on purpose.<br /> <br /> <u>Mudra Mudra</u>: This is just the <u>Arcane Focus</u> ritual for the Talisman but fluffed differently.<br /> <br /> <u>Actual Geomancy This Time</u>: Battery Hearthstone.<br /> Motes: +1 per turn in a Manse. Once per story 5sm for emptying a hearthstone, 10 for a greater one. Hearthstones are depowered until the end of the story.<br /> Control: No<br /> Opinion: I guess I should evaluate these by the lowered standards of Deebs, but even then, its pretty weak.<br /> Verdict: pitifully weak. Like Dynasts. (Solars4Lyfe ride or die)<br /> <br /> <b>Wanasaan Exorcist</b>: Something about drowning.<br /> <br /> <u>Paper Tiger</u>: Sacrifice something to yourself to placate your own ghost...?<br /> Motes: destroy (Resources) effigy to get (Resources) sm for the day.<br /> Control: No<br /> Opinion: for this to ever matter you need to be R4 or R5.<br /> Verdict: No.<br /> <br /> <u>Drown Yourself</u>: Meditate underwater to get motes.<br /> Motes: (Wits+Occult) after 1 hour of meditation. Lasts for story or until you meditate again. Limit once per day.<br /> Control: No<br /> Opinion: Oh hey, easily bankable, excellency-able sm's. The best and most OP kind. This is better than any of the Solar Rituals. The ease of use + the lack of any meaningful restrictions are what makes this very strong. Compare it with <u>Protein Shake</u> from the Alchemy rituals to see what I mean.<br /> Verdict: Best Ritual in the game.<br /> <br /> (Metal Gear Solid 3) <u>Ghost Eater</u>: fix a ghost's unfinished business.<br /> Motes: Roll (Stam+Occult+ Ghost's Essence) after you fix a ghost's unfinished business. Maxes out at (I stopped caring) motes. ([Ess+WP]x4)<br /> Control: I guess we just arent doing this in WFHW<br /> Opinion: you REALLY have to commit to helping Casper move on for this to matter. The high maximum is offset by how hard it is to build up.<br /> Verdict: Take this for RP, its almost useless otherwise.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <u>FANGS AT THE GATE</u><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Raksi's Tutelage</b>: Notice me, Senpai!<br /> <br /> <i>Side note: </i>so now that it's Book 3 all the shaping rituals have cool names. Way to ruin my fun, devs.<br /> <br /> <u>Balancing on the Edge</u>: The Same, But More<br /> Motes: 0. Yeah, this ritual actually lets you repeat you shape sorcery roll to do the same sorcery again but tweaked in a different way. Limit once per story<br /> Control: Get the bennies you got the first time round.<br /> Opinion: the effects are pretty open ended but you have to make a whole new Shape Sorcery roll, so it aint happening soon. I'm actually not sure if the first spell happens right away or you have to wait until the second roll is done too.<br /> Verdict: I have no idea. Somebody else can take this one.<br /> <br /> <u>Sigil-Skin Geometry</u>: Power Tattoos!<br /> Motes: (Int+ Linguistics or Lore) against Diff 2. Extra successes are motes. Can only do one spell at a time. Limit to one spell per day. It doesn't expire though, you keep it until you use it.<br /> Control: add (Ess or 3) noncharm dice, whichever is higher.<br /> Opinion: Remember what I said about Excellencies, bankabitily, and OP? Well here you go. The \u201cdrawback\u201d is that it only works on one spell at a time, but you only need (and probably only have) one combat spell at a time anyway.<br /> Verdict: The Second Best Ritual in the Game.<br /> <br /> <u>Terror Relishing Art</u>: Scare people, get motes<br /> Motes: After you succeed on a roll to Threaten/Inspire Fear, gain (Attribute Used) motes for the scene. If they are a higher Essence than you, gain the difference in your Essence. So this will usually be 5sm, sometime 6 or 7,<br /> Control: none<br /> Opinion: I've seen the Lunar Terror build, but this is niche even for that. Will probably make for cool Trex rp stunts though.<br /> Verdict: This is more of a \u201ccool\u201d Ritual than a \u201cGood\u201d ritual. But if you wanna feel like a badass you could do worse.<br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine Gems of Mishiko</b>: All the nonsense koans you can shake a crystal flower at.<br /> <br /> <u>Remembrance of Mishiko</u>: Sacrifice Resources and use a Perf\u2026. wait a minute<br /> Opinion: this is literally the \u201cBurnt Offerings\u201d Ritual refluffed.<br /> <br /> <u>Sorcerer's Quest</u>: Follow the plotted line.<br /> Motes: you get one motes for each piece of candy you find in the woods, up to 10sm, which last for the story. The ST is supposed to put these infront of you like mini plot hooks. Also, if you have an Intimacy that ties into a place where you find the Forbidden Sorcerer Candy, you get (Ess x 2/3/4) sm until you leave that place.<br /> Control: Nope.<br /> Opinion: This is the Plot Hook ritual, where you are supposed to hear about the crystal flowers and then go get them like collectibles in a video game. It might get shoehorny real fast, or it might be awesome, heavily ST dependent.<br /> Verdict: Mechanically weak. I have to admit a bias though- I love flowers, crystals, and adventure so I actually like this one for reason aside from its usefulness.<br /> <br /> <u>Twilight Koan</u>: Riddle Me This, Lunar-Man<br /> Motes: (Higher of Lore or Int) sm which last for a scene, so basically 5sm.<br /> Control: No.<br /> Opinion:does that mean they only last for the scene you get them in? I would think RAI no, but, we'll just say they carry over into the next \u201creal\u201d scene. Get these motes Morning and Evening. Its kinda silly, but at least you get to show off your nonsense koan abilities to everyone.<br /> Verdict: a free 5sm just for existing isn't bad, but it's not nearly as good as some others.<br /> <br /> <b>Root Lore</b>: Druids in Exalted<br /> <br /> <u>Master Apothecary Enlightenment</u>: Introduce a fact, heal someone, or use craft, to get SM<br /> Motes: (Int + Extra Successes) on the plant fact or healing roll. That could be very big. (Int+ Silver Points+[Gold Pointsx2]) on the crafting roll. Could be biggish. Story length, can only use one or the other effect, they don't stack<br /> Control: no<br /> Opinion: This is rewarding proactive character play with motes, this is how all rituals should be designed. The motes are both Excellenciable and Storable, the best combo of all.<br /> Verdict: Amazing. This is probably the best designed ritual in the game.<br /> <br /> <u>Sorcerer's Harvest</u>: Tap a Forest for Green Mana<br /> Motes: (Essence) from a big plant. Hey isnt this....<br /> Yeah this is the same as <u>Fueled By Fire</u>, but plants this time.<br /> <br /> <u>Thousand Bloom Arts</u>: Unlimited Plant Works.<br /> Motes: once per scene, you can get highest of (Int, Lore, or Survival), so basically 5sm.<br /> Control: No<br /> Opinion: This requires a Diff 2 (Int+Survival) roll to find plants enough for one casting, or Diff 4 to get a whole weeks worth. Does this remind you of <u>Protein Shake</u>? The difference here is that bonus successes do not become SMs. The difficulty is basically non-existant because you are certain to throw like 20 dice at this, so its more like \u201conce a week, remind people you are an herbalist, always have 5sm on hand\u201d<br /> Verdict: A lot like <u>Twilight Koan</u>, this is basically just giving you SM for existing. You could do worse than a flat 5sm once per scene, so it's probably the most middle-rank, Benchmarkable ritual in the book. Its slightly better than <u>Twilight Koan</u> too, because if you do the Difficulty 4 roll you have enough plants for multiple scenes per day, unlike those zen dweebs who have to wait until nighttime.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Summary: Far and away, the best Shaping Rituals are those that that you use an Excellency in your downtime (where spent motes essentially have no cost) to store Sorcery Motes.<br /> <br /> <u>Most Powerful Ritual</u>: <b>Wanasaan Exorcist's</b> <u>Drown Self</u> ritual. It's a simple (Wits+Occ) roll that you can full excellency and Charm, there's no difficulty to beat, and the motes last for the story. You just need an hour of downtime and some water. The only drawback is needing to go underwater again to use it. Obviously it becomes weaker the more Sorcery you need to cast in a single day, but the trade off is worth it.<br /> Runner Up: <u>Sigil Skin Geometry</u>, which is very similar.<br /> <br /> <u>Best Designed Ritual</u>: <b>Root Lore's</b> <u>Master Apothecary Enlightenment</u>. Encourages proactive use of a certain playstyle, while also offering a lot of power.<br /> Runner Up: <u>Dark Dreams</u>, which has a great tradeoff for power.<br /> <br /> <u>Most OP Ritua</u>l: <b>The Talisman's </b><u>I See You</u>, for giving you free sm on a roll you're heavily incentivized to max out anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Hey, Overlord, why isn't Most OP the same as Most Powerful?</i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Because of the way SM come to you. <u>I See You</u> is the Single Point of Rituals- its a winmore added to mechanics the game already wants you to be disgustingly good at, for no cost because it's a free generated effect. If you are going to play a combat monster this is the Ritual for you. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <u>Worst Ritual In The Game</u>: <b>Bargain With Mara's </b><u>Sex Vampire</u>. It gets you 0 motes because I won't play with anyone who has it.<br /> <br /> <u>The Benchmark Rituals</u>: <b>Mishiko's </b><u>Twilight Koan</u> gives you 5sm at dawn and dusk, no rolls or anything required. <b>Root Lore's </b><u>Thousand Bloom Arts</u> gives you 5sm every scene as long as you can find plants <i>once per week</i>. These two are basically the \u201cHave 5sm on hand just for existing\u201d rituals. If any ritual is weaker than this, its weak. If it's more powerful than this with no drawback, its strong.<br /> <br /> TL;DR- Excellencies are OP.<br /> <br /> Whew! Thank you for reading this. It took me several hours and 9 pages to type out. My way to give back to the community. I hope there's some good discussion here.<br /> <br /> Edit: I misread <u>Protein Shake</u> and had thought extra successes got in there somehow. It's fixed now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 06-13-2020, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T19:14:22-07:00","id":1396098,"title":"","content":"I think the Balancing on the Edge ritual is not meant to cast a second spell - it's meant to let you roll two Shape Sorcery rolls in one turn for the same spell, by making the spell do more collateral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T20:21:56-07:00","id":1396104,"title":"","content":"Cool list!<br /> <br /> I have the heptagram one and it doesn't suck in our game. It takes place in a large city so there is a library around, so it's not hard to go there between major fights. It may not be as good as the other excellency-able ones but it's viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T20:46:17-07:00","id":1396108,"title":"","content":"I think you might be sleeping a bit on Deranged in scarred by nightmares. If you are built around a single control spell (like say you're a Brilliant Raptor sniper or something) then that is +4sm every action for something you would have stunted anyway, it isn't as immediately impactful as maybe protein shake, but over even a single combat you probably rack the motes up really quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 06-13-2020, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T04:00:21-07:00","id":1396149,"title":"","content":"You know that it's possible to have unrequited love without sex, right?<br /> <br /> Just see... moooosst fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T05:18:49-07:00","id":1396159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power#post1396094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Soul Perfecting Elixir's</b> <u>Protein Shake</u> is stupid good. The only reason its not better than <u>Drown Self</u> is that you trade the<b><span style=\"color:#FF8C00\"> successes lost to Difficulty 4 </span></b>for the ability to use it for a whole week.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power#post1396094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Protein Shake</u>: Get mana from alchemical Bro Science<br /> Motes: another complicated one. Difficulty 2 (Int+Craft) roll to make a potion, <b><span style=\"color:#FF8C00\">bonus successes give you sm.</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>In my version of the book, drinking the resultant potion is a miscellaneous Stamina + Occult action which gives you successes in sorc-motes. Is this some sort of errata I didn't get yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10091-altasaire","name":"Altasaire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T05:21:37-07:00","id":1396160,"title":"","content":"I think you may be misinterpreting Protein Shake - it looks to me like the sorcerous motes are based on a stamina+occult roll you make when you drink it, not the int+craft roll you make to brew it.<br /> Which makes it significantly worse, since you can't use craft charms and any excellency use comes in the middle of a scene were you are doing other stuff.<br /> Also, the requirement to spend an action drinking it is important - it means the fastest you can cast a spell is 2 actions, 1 to drink and 1 to shape sorcery (unless you read it as possible to cast a spell without ever taking a shape sorcery action), and in my experience &quot;optimizing shaping rituals for casting one spell&quot; has the goal of casting the spell in 1 action, and quickly can treat casting it in two actions as trivial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:10:47-07:00","id":1396231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1396149#post1396149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know that it's possible to have unrequited love without sex, right?<br /> <br /> Just see... moooosst fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, actually. It had never occurred to me. What a concept. <br /> <br /> Which is why i said you need a pc to agree to have unrequited love for you, or you have npc allies/mentor/retainer on hand who has unrequited love for you. And since Someone literally defined by their love for you only gives 4 sm, once per scene. If you want that Ritual to work well you are encouraged to have a gaggle of them. <br /> <br /> I'm sure someone could maturely roleplay having several lovestruck followers on hand all the time, but that's right on the edge of &quot;I made an npc harem&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:14:49-07:00","id":1396234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1396098#post1396098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Balancing on the Edge ritual is not meant to cast a second spell - it's meant to let you roll two Shape Sorcery rolls in one turn for the same spell, by making the spell do more collateral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. I couldn't wrap my head around the timing and when the spells go off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T16:25:23-07:00","id":1396240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1396108#post1396108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you might be sleeping a bit on Deranged in scarred by nightmares. If you are built around a single control spell (like say you're a Brilliant Raptor sniper or something) then that is +4sm every action for something you would have stunted anyway, it isn't as immediately impactful as maybe protein shake, but over even a single combat you probably rack the motes up really quick.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly a valid take on it, and if you are the kind of Sorcerer who wants to rely on Spells in combat than having a perpetual mote generator can be good- i mentioned that in the 10k eyes section. But that's not the way I've seen most Sorcerers operate so I graded rituals for how useful they are to get off your first spell.<br /> <br /> As Always, Your Mileage May Vary.<br /> <br /> (Also sorry about the multiposts, I'm mobile atm and multi quote formatting is a nightmare)<br /> <br /> <b>Protein Shake has been fixed. Don't know how that slipped through. </b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 06-13-2020, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T08:28:04-07:00","id":1396392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1396234#post1396234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly. I couldn't wrap my head around the timing and when the spells go off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's just a single spell. &quot;Shape Sorcery&quot; is any roll you make towards gathering SM. The timing is &quot;Make a Shape Sorcery roll. If that doesn't cut it for a spell, make a second Shape Sorcery roll while declaring a side effect. That likely causes the spell to go off by then.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:34:45-07:00","id":1396414,"title":"","content":"I'm still critical, but I do honestly feel apologetic for the patronising manner in which I made that point. So I apologise for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1396231#post1396231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why i said you need a pc to agree to have unrequited love for you, or you have npc allies/mentor/retainer on hand who has unrequited love for you. And since Someone literally defined by their love for you only gives 4 sm, once per scene. If you want that Ritual to work well you are encouraged to have a gaggle of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you see as the practical value of shaping rituals? Do you intend them as a resource to call upon for practically every spell, and to do most of the heavy lifting of powering them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure someone could maturely roleplay having several lovestruck followers on hand all the time, but that's right on the edge of &amp;quot;I made an npc harem&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire game of Exalted constantly hovers on the edge of absurdity, and has since the beginning. I'm tempted to make a snide, possibly elitist comment about that fact, but I'm held back right now by consideration for how that space and the discourse around it has always been a significant generator of enthusiasm for the game.<br /> <br /> I shall instead settle upon the point that I found your prior phrasing to be reductive in a manner that weakens your assessment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T15:21:00-07:00","id":1396503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1396414#post1396414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still critical, but I do honestly feel apologetic for the patronising manner in which I made that point. So I apologise for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's cool. I accept your apology. I apologize for snarking back. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What do you see as the practical value of shaping rituals? Do you intend them as a resource to call upon for practically every spell, and to do most of the heavy lifting of powering them? </div> </div> </div><i>CAVEAT: There is an assumption with this rating system: the ability to quickly cast your first in-combat Sorcery is much more important than your ability to get off your second or third spell in the scene.</i><br /> <br /> The practical job of the Shaping Ritual is to get your Spell off as soon as possible, preferably in one turn. As I clarified in the beginning, most Sorcerers use 1 incombat spell fueled by their Ritual and then switch to charms. <br /> <br /> So back to Unrequited Love, you would need 3 or more people, <b>defined by their love for you</b> to blow more than 10 motes on your control spell. It's possible. In a vacuum, that could even be really powerful\u2026 <br /> <br /> But then the Grim Spectre of Table Play rears its head. Toting around 3 people who love you so much it defines their being has some unfortunate baggage. It can easily turn into bad table etiquette/That Guyism to keep them around and rp them. <br /> <br /> And not for nothing, but this Ritual is from Mara. The design space is clearly broadcasting &quot;be an abuser for power&quot;, and I don't think anyone needs it spelled out why that might ruin the fun for others at the table. It would at mine. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The entire game of Exalted constantly hovers on the edge of absurdity, and has since the beginning. I'm tempted to make a snide, possibly elitist comment about that fact, but I'm held back right now by consideration for how that space and the discourse around it has always been a significant generator of enthusiasm for the game. </div> </div> </div>Weird that you open with an apology and then drop a &quot;I could belittle you, but I won't&quot;. Honestly we both know where this ends: a derailed thread about Mara and Sex and Love and stuff. I don't want that on a thread i put hours of effort into. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I shall instead settle upon the point that I found your prior phrasing to be reductive in a manner that weakens your assessment. </div> </div> </div>And I find purple patches to not a nice garment make, nor length increase rhetorical strength. <br /> <br /> We're all adults here. Nobody needs it exhaustively spelled out why toting a harem around is a bad idea. If it works for you and your table, great! Have fun. But I don't like where it leads and I'm not going to discuss the matter here any further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T20:10:10-07:00","id":1396595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1396503#post1396503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>CAVEAT: There is an assumption with this rating system: the ability to quickly cast your first in-combat Sorcery is much more important than your ability to get off your second or third spell in the scene.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes. I did overlook that.<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> think it's a particularly narrow avenue within which to assess sorcery, and that many shaping rituals are particularly not designed towards facilitating it.<br /> <br /> Indeed, dedicated combat sorcerers probably want initiations particularly themed towards combat.<br /> <br /> But even then, I feel as though the good rituals do not supercede the shape sorcery action, they merely ease it along. The need to shape a spell over time unless deliberate actions or fortunate circumstances line up an especially good flow of motes feels integral to the aesthetic of sorcery to me. To whit, even Mara's disciple gets something out of stringing a person along so that their Brilliant Raptor takes a few less seconds to pull together.<br /> <br /> The priority for me would be immersion in what quirks are introduced to the personality by initiations. Maybe somebody taught by Mara is ruthless enough to want to bring around multiple people, maybe they're aren't. Maybe they are but it's just too damn impractical.<br /> <br /> I don't think the complications are incorrect, but I think there's something something to be said for embracing the struggles of them. Not for you specifically, just not to be written off from the outset.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And not for nothing, but this Ritual is from Mara. The design space is clearly broadcasting &amp;quot;be an abuser for power&amp;quot;, and I don't think anyone needs it spelled out why that might ruin the fun for others at the table. It would at mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>As unrequited love goes, there <i>is</i> another approach.<br /> <br /> In fiction and probably in real life, unrequited love is uncommonly depicted as something that was deliberately cultivated for the sake of cruelty. One person can be deeply compelling to another, without reciprocating their feelings. To not reciprocate is not abusive. To move on if rejected is smart, and often failed at, if the attempt was even made.<br /> <br /> A Storyteller ought to accommodate the player who wants to explore that narrative while also utilizing it more optimally but not wanting to be deeply compromised.<br /> <br /> And it can make sense for Mara to teach a person who'll break many hearts while not wanting to, to grant a source of power that will provoke torment over the ethical question of using opportunistically. Mara loves dark destinies, she does not necessarily care about agency within them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird that you open with an apology</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote that post out of order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">then drop a &amp;quot;I could belittle you, but I won't&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not about you, that's about records of the First Edition fandom and me openly telling myself off for being a prick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I find purple patches to not a nice garment make, nor length increase rhetorical strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just how I speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody needs it exhaustively spelled out why toting a harem around is a bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your strict characterisation of that as a harem is what I am referring to as reductive.<br /> <br /> (I do mean to express thoughts about the other assessments of shaping rituals)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-14-2020, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T20:41:50-07:00","id":1396597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1396595#post1396595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah yes. I did overlook that.<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> think it's a particularly narrow avenue within which to assess sorcery, and that many shaping rituals are particularly not designed towards facilitating it.<br /> <br /> Indeed, dedicated combat sorcerers probably want initiations particularly themed towards combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you're not a combat sorcerer, your shaping ritual is mainly going to come up in gameplay during combat. If you're using spells outside of combat, then the time to shape is almost never a concern.<br /> <br /> Of course you can flavor your out-of-combat spell-shaping as involving the shaping ritual, but you don't really need a table to evaluate shaping rituals for that purpose - just pick the one that sounds cool to you. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T02:22:16-07:00","id":1396630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1396597#post1396597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're using spells outside of combat, then the time to shape is almost never a concern.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it ought to be portrayed as time in which other characters can react, not least of which are countering sorcerers.<br /> <br /> That and I wonder if there are not players who would prefer to not spend too much time rolling towards performing a single action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T04:03:34-07:00","id":1396641,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> I'm sorry if I got too heated in my last comment. You're cool, I'm cool. <br /> <br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25834\" data-vbnamecard=\"25834\">habitableexoplanet</a>, Shaping Rituals only (Mechanically!) matter in combat, or when time is of the immediate essence, which is functionally very similar. So I heavily scored towards that metric. <br /> <br /> And other stuff aside, a Shaping Ritual that relies on keeping NPC's Intimacies is difficult to manage, and they have to be within Medium Range, and you can only use multiple people at once for your Control Spell, and there's a hard Limit of 10 motes per Scene. Compared to Wanasaan's Drowning Ritual, you can easily get 10 motes via excellency the night before and use them without restrictions. Mara's Intimacy Ritual does open the door for a lot of RP, but the mechanics are inferior to Drowning. <br /> <br /> There's also a realization I didn't have until today: These people have to be withing medium range of you. Which means that, in combat, they are going to be <i>In combat</i>. It's not impossible that they are good at it, but... Followers, Retainers, and Allies can die. It's just a lot of dishes to keep spinning for relatively few motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T05:18:43-07:00","id":1396650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1396630#post1396630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it ought to be portrayed as time in which other characters can react, not least of which are countering sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you commonly in a scenario where other characters want to react negatively to spellcasting, and in particular counterspell outside of combat? This has never happened to me. I would think that when enemies of the type who want to counter your spells are around, you would quickly proceed to combat.<br /> <br /> I guess maybe this could happen with some of the social spells, like Corrupted Words, but that's the only spell in the core book where that seems likely to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That and I wonder if there are not players who would prefer to not spend too much time rolling towards performing a single action. </div> </div> </div>I don't think you're really supposed to roll for it when a few combat rounds of time isn't a concern. Shape Sorcery is described as a combat action in the books.<br /> <br /> Using a shaping ritual just to avoid rolling is a very dangerous game because almost all have per-day or per-story limits, so it leaves you unprepared for a future scenario where time is of the essence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T05:58:24-07:00","id":1396655,"title":"","content":"Eating Mental Anguish may be a little better depending how liberally you interpret the text. It puts a strong emphasis on emotions, which is not entirely covered by intimacies and limit. Inspire actions have very similar effects, are literally pure emotion overflowing, emulate intimacies for some purposes (it takes the place of a major intimacy to help/hinder persuasions) and are much easier to pull in combat.<br /> <br /> A social character can reasonably pull this off in combat unless every party involved pays the wp (which is not a waste! especially if you combo to expect that like a Nightingale practicioner). It's an easy 3sm per scene on top of whatever else you had.<br /> <br /> This segways into...<br /> <br /> <br /> Action expenditure has a bit more nuance than you are accounting, and it's an important one for combat. Any ritual-backed sm gain counts as your shape sorcery action. This has two benefits.<br /> 1) This frees you to use some other action without losing sm (sometimes the angry tyrant lizard has an angrier mate and your circle's busy with the first one a couple range bands away)<br /> 2) If you bank enough sm this is a way to cast &quot;reflexively&quot;. This is limited for a terrestrial sorcerer, but a celestial or solar sorcerer can have pre-banked motes on top of this ritual and really make it shine.<br /> <br /> For example, Burning Passion. Your overhyped swashbuckler finally got to deliver his &quot;You killed my father, time to die&quot; speech to the trio of DBs that, well, killed your father. When you deal a killing blow to one of them the DM says you have gained 1wp from upholding your tie of hate towards the trio. Bam, 5sm. But wait! You already had 2sm leftover from a previous invocation of Burning Passion! Or maybe you had shaped those motes when attacking wasn't opportune (damn ninja's trying to kite you!). Instant Mists of Eventide!<br /> <br /> And yes this makes I See You even grosser. Burning 3-4 wp on JB through awakening eye and this ritual is cheap considering the spell will be out before you even act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T16:40:28-07:00","id":1396967,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested to hear how you rate some of the initiations and shaping rituals provided in the Heirs to the Shogunate preview (i.e., Simendor Sorcery, the Valkhawsen Way, and Student of the Sixfold Insight). The Talismanic Focus ritual of the Valkhawsen Way in particular seemed like a viable one for combat sorcery, to me at least.<br /> <br /> Also, although I realize it may not be canon, the Sorcerous Ways product on Storyteller's Vault had an initiation I found particularly interesting for combat sorcerers, namely <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts?term=sorcerou&amp;filters=0_0_45735_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Mystic Martial Arts</a>, which I think deserve a look. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T06:27:20-07:00","id":1397078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sadric of Ysyr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1396967#post1396967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be interested to hear how you rate some of the initiations and shaping rituals provided in the Heirs to the Shogunate preview (i.e., Simendor Sorcery, the Valkhawsen Way, and Student of the Sixfold Insight). The Talismanic Focus ritual of the Valkhawsen Way in particular seemed like a viable one for combat sorcery, to me at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where in the previews are those? Did part 3 come out without me noticing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T07:32:17-07:00","id":1397086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1397078#post1397078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where in the previews are those? Did part 3 come out without me noticing?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're dotted through part one so easily missed:<br /> <br /> Simendor Sorcery is on page 14<br /> <br /> The Valkhawsen Way is on page 52<br /> <br /> Student of the Sixfold Insight is on page 75","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T18:52:49-07:00","id":1397189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1397086#post1397086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're dotted through part one so easily missed:<br /> <br /> Simendor Sorcery is on page 14<br /> <br /> The Valkhawsen Way is on page 52<br /> <br /> Student of the Sixfold Insight is on page 75</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. OH. Really weird that they would do that. Valkhawsen seems really fucking good: Empty-Mind is excellency-able, bankable, difficulty 0, lasts the whole story and can be renewed every day. It even gives you flexibility regarding which ability you want to use for the roll. Talismanic Focus, on the other hand, is basically +3 non-charm successes to every shape sorcery roll always and for basically no cost. So for both the &quot;get my one big spell ASAP&quot; and &quot;Brilliant Raptor Machinegun&quot; flavours of sorcerer it's the Valkhawsen Way or the highway. Plus the Enlightened Contemplation merit is really good too.<br /> <br /> None of the others really stand out, but I could imagine a super gimmicky build for a Sixfold Insight Student with Enlightenment Through Adversity and Lens of Austerity who flagellates themselves into their -2s and gets high on snake venom before going into battle and spams +8sm on each roll while screaming about the Emperor or something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T19:12:46-07:00","id":1397196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396094-shaping-rituals-and-you-a-guide-to-power?p=1397189#post1397189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh. OH. Really weird that they would do that. Valkhawsen seems really fucking good: Empty-Mind is excellency-able, bankable, difficulty 0, lasts the whole story and can be renewed every day. It even gives you flexibility regarding which ability you want to use for the roll. Talismanic Focus, on the other hand, is basically +3 non-charm successes to every shape sorcery roll always and for basically no cost. So for both the &quot;get my one big spell ASAP&quot; and &quot;Brilliant Raptor Machinegun&quot; flavours of sorcerer it's the Valkhawsen Way or the highway. Plus the Enlightened Contemplation merit is really good too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talismanic Focus is once per scene, I think, which makes it very bad IMO.<br /> <br /> Agree 100% on Empty-Mind and Enlightened Contemplation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T23:02:37-07:00","id":1397899,"title":"","content":"It seems worth noting for the &quot;Eating Mental Anguish&quot; that while the limit effect is obviously restricted to people with a Limit track, the Intimacy effect works on <i>anyone </i>around, which means you can trigger it just by sticking Minors on random people you meet (which I take as intentional, since it's meant to make you more raksha-like). So you can instill, but you don't even need to go that far -- if anyone threatens anyone else, that will usually create a negative emotional Intimacy, as in many cases will doing something unpleasant in a large group. I'm using this one in a game right now and while it's early on, my impression is that you can make it work pretty well even if the rest of your party isn't helpful, but you have to actively hustle to try to make it ping in as many scenes as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}